{"profile":{"name":"Anthony Perruzza","ward":"Ward 7, Humber River-Black Creek","bio":"Serving on Toronto City Council since 2006, representing Ward 8 York West from 2006 to 2018 and Ward 7 Humber River-Black Creek since the 2018 ward amalgamation, re-elected in 2022. Earlier he was a trustee on the Metro Toronto Separate School Board (1985-88), a North York city councillor (1988-90), and a Member of Provincial Parliament for Downsview (1990-95); he ran for mayor of Toronto in the 2023 by-election. He is seeking re-election in the 2026 municipal election.","committees":["Infrastructure and Environment Committee","Etobicoke & York Community Council (Vice-Chair)","Toronto Community Housing Corporation Board of Directors","Exhibition Place Board of Governors","Hockey Hall of Fame Board of Directors","Toronto and Region Conservation Authority (Executive Member, Partners in Project Green Executive Management Committee)"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_perruzza@toronto.ca","phone":"416-338-5335"},"promises":[{"text":"Signed the Toronto Environmental Alliance's Greener City for All election pledge in 2022, committing to support priority actions including fully funding Toronto's climate strategy (2025/2030/2040 targets), overhauling heating and cooling bylaws and a fair stormwater charge for climate resilience, and regulations to eliminate unnecessary single-use items toward a zero-waste city.","source":"http://election.torontoenvironment.org/pledge_results"},{"text":"In his 2026 re-election campaign, his stated priorities are affordability, continued investment in infrastructure, essential services and value for taxpayers, with focus on roads, sewers, parks, playgrounds, transit, housing and support for seniors.","source":"https://www.downsviewadvocate.ca/news/municipal-election"}]},"lobbying":{"total":897,"term":198,"first":"2010-08-24","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":233,"clients":197,"subjects":444,"methods":{"Meetings":254,"Emails":477,"Phone calls":49,"Written":84,"Ot